# A pipe at the end of a statement: DS0103. Removing it may not be what was meant, so the fix is not machine-applicable.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | take 5 |;
from 'customers.csv' | count
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..59
  PIPELINE@0..28
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    TAKE_OP@20..26
      IDENT@20..24 "take"
      WHITESPACE@24..25 " "
      LITERAL@25..26
        LONG@25..26 "5"
    WHITESPACE@26..27 " "
    PIPE@27..28 "|"
  SEMICOLON@28..29 ";"
  WHITESPACE@29..30 "\n"
  PIPELINE@30..58
    IDENT@30..34 "from"
    WHITESPACE@34..35 " "
    LITERAL@35..50
      STRING@35..50 "'customers.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@50..51 " "
    PIPE@51..52 "|"
    WHITESPACE@52..53 " "
    COUNT_OP@53..58
      IDENT@53..58 "count"
  WHITESPACE@58..59 "\n"

error[DS0103]: `|` with no operator after it
  --> query:1:28
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | take 5 |;
  |                            ^ expected an operator after this `|`
  |
  = help: remove the `|`, or add an operator after it, such as `take 10`
